  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trinidad &amp; Tobago Kigali Implementation Plan Stage 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the Intersessional Approval Process for the 93rd meeting of the Executive Committee (ExCom) held in December 2023, through of the document 93/89, the ExCom approved the Kigali Implementation Plan Stage I (KIP I) for Trinidad and Tobago for the period 2024 to 2029 to reduce HFC consumption by 10% (568,178 CO2-eq tonnes) of the country&#x2019;s baseline (5,681,787 CO2-eq tonnes). Stage I of the KIP will reduce 10% of the HFCs consumption by 2029. This project will be financed with US $1,177,695 plus a</narrative>
  </description>
